.venv/
tests/
shoreline/
# The predecessor bot's source, kept locally as a reference. 33 MB the build
# context has no use for -- the Dockerfile's COPY lines name everything the
# image needs, so this only ever cost upload time to the daemon.
old mergebot-main/
# Source art for the Discord app emoji, uploaded to the bot application by hand
# rather than read at runtime -- polybot references them by the ID Discord hands
# back (<:wolfyay:...>), never by path, so the image has no use for the ~3.8MB of
# PNGs and the .xcf beside them. They stay in the repo because that upload is a
# manual step and the originals have to live somewhere.
Emojis/
__pycache__/
.idea/
.claude/
.env

# The repository history, and by a wide margin the largest thing in the
# context: 119 MB against the 33 MB of `old mergebot-main/` above, which is
# excluded for exactly this reason. Nothing COPYs it and no build step reads it.
.git/
.github/
# Development-only, and none of it is COPYd: the baseline harness and probes,
# the design notes, the superseded merge script, a local baseline snapshot, and
# the public mirror's README.
tools/
publish/
CLAUDE.md
polymerge_old.py
before.json

# There is deliberately no `*.png` rule here any more, and it must not come
# back. It existed to keep the ~100MB of test screenshots out of the context,
# but `tests/` and `shoreline/` already do that wholesale -- and it carried
# exceptions for two board renders that have since been deleted, so with the
# rule in place `COPY Overlays/` and `COPY Assets/` would have matched
# *nothing* and built an image with no board renders and no ruin sprite. See
# the Dockerfile's COPY block for what that cost.
#
# Everything the image needs is named explicitly by COPY, so this file only has
# to keep the context small.
